title: Your waiter is right; the root note's lines on the pacer should say not to restart it by 'kill'.
pid: 595e6d61-fd43-480d-8d79-eb5155deb610
body: |2-
  The waiter ('stop', then wait on the pid, then 'exec ... run') is the
  safe way and needs no change. What is untrue or missing in your notes:
  the note on restarting the pacer (5a92324a) says it is done "from
  inside a session it started"; from any other session it is the same
  'stop' and waiter, and 'kill' must not be used, since it orphans the
  session. 'pacer.sh status' no longer prints "running (pid N)" but
  "running: the pacer (pid N, started T)", if anything of yours greps it.
